.********************************************************************
.* GENERAL COMMAND HELP TEXT
.*
:HELP NAME=ANLSRCF.
Analyse source files - Help
:P.
The :CIT.ANLSRCF:ECIT. command is used to scan source
files of all or selected types for specified character
strings (max. 10) and to print them in a report.
:P.
It's always helpful if you have to search for certain
source code in "unknown" locations.
:P.
:EHELP.
.********************************************************************
.* HELP TEXT for Parameter: SRCFILE
.*
:HELP NAME='ANLSRCF/SRCFILE'.
Source file (SRCFILE) - Help
:P.
:XH3.SRCFILE (Source file)
:P.
Specifies name and library of the source file(s)
to be used for search.
:P.
This is a required parameter.
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.Name
:PD.Source file name
:PT.*RPG
:PD.Selects all members from type RPG/RPGLE.
:PT.*CL
:PD.Selects all members from type CLP/CLLE.
:PT.*CMD
:PD.Selects all members from type CMD.
:PT.*ALL
:PD.Selects source file members of all types.
:EPARML.
:P.
The possible library values are:
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.library-name
:PD.Specify the library where the file is located.
:PT.*ALLUSR
:PD.All user libraries are searched for the source file(s).
:PT.generic* library  name
:PD.Type a partial library name qualified by an asterisk (*) to
select a specific subset of libraries.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
.********************************************************************
.* HELP TEXT for Parameter: STRING_1
.*
:HELP NAME='ANLSRCF/STRING_1'.
Search string 1 (STRING_1) - Help
:P.
:XH3.STRING_1 (Search string 1)
:P.
Enter one of max. 10 character strings which are to be
searched for.
:EHELP.
